{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/526192-have-you-run-owod-setting-with-nwod-2e-rules-tell-us-about-it-here","id":526192,"title":"Have you run oWoD setting with nWoD 2E rules? Tell us about it here!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T18:37:17-07:00","id":526192,"title":"Have you run oWoD setting with nWoD 2E rules? Tell us about it here!","content":"I have been wanting to do a game set in the Old World but using the New World 2E rules. I'm curious who has done this and how it turned out. Post your rules, your game information, your general ideas here (even if you haven't run such a game yet!). Some of the games seem easier to convert than others. <b>Masquerade </b>to <b>Requiem </b>is pretty easy. I just use Blood Potency, with it being a general measure of Generation\u2014increased through diablerie as usual. I'm considering letting it increase like it does normally in <b>Requiem </b>or with Experiences (you can experiment, strengthen the Beast and your mastery of the Blood, etc.), with Generation being more of a roleplaying concern than a hard cap on potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf </b>isn't too bad; generally what I do is take the <b>Forsaken </b>2E forms and remove the limits on Gauru (and its increased healing), keep the general Forsaken template, and Gifts can stay largely the same. Those that are important in <b>Apocalypse </b>but not present can be converted fairly easily. A lot of the Fera use similar stuff, or somewhat modified forms. I even created a list of nWoD 2E-compatible Archid traits for the Mokol\u00e9.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage </b>I'm really not sure about. I vastly prefer <b>Awakening </b>and its magic system, but I want to keep the general fluff and &quot;feel&quot; of <b>Ascension </b>for oWoD-based games. This one I'm not at all sure how to convert. <b>Changeling </b>seems like it might not be <i>too </i>hard, and relies more on description than anything, but the chimeric reality and Dreaming stuff could be difficult.<br /> <br /> So, let's hear your thoughts on doing any and every oWoD game with nWoD 2E rules!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T00:20:20-07:00","id":530727,"title":"","content":"there is a conversion book on pdf for all three major game lines including mage. that should help you convert the magic rules. If your going for the feel of mage: the ascension i strongly recommend you use the &quot;ascension capabilities&quot; rather than the &quot;awakening practices&quot;. Awakening magic is built around a single truth that every mage utilizes regardless of style. Ascension's &quot;truth&quot; and reality are subjective to individual beliefs and unless your planning on an all hermetic game, the Awakening system just doesn't really capture the vibe of Ascension. Magic works really different in both games and their systems reflect that. that's just my two cents others will probably disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:41:50-07:00","id":538292,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by awakening practices? If I was to do a conversion (still trying to decide whether or not to do so) i would just have the dot ratings and dice pools come from awakening (rename gnosis arete, then do arete+arcana) but everything still comes from your paradigm. You need a foci and it has to fit within your paradigm in order to do it. Probably also split up entropy and correspondence into space, death, and fate. Rote dice pools are determined by your paradigm if you are well practiced in using that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T07:43:48-07:00","id":538295,"title":"","content":"For vampire, I would do what a local LARP did and use both blood potency and generation where low generation makes blood potency cheaper and high generation makes blood potency prohibitively expensive but still buyable. Otherwise, there is not a huge amount to change. You would have to redesign some diciplines but might use that blood magic book as a starting point for converting necromancy and Tremere sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:40:43-07:00","id":543110,"title":"","content":"One thing I have thought of doing was doing an all order of hermes game using awakenings ruleset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:07:59-07:00","id":543939,"title":"","content":"Awakening has a heaping dose of Theosophism mixed in with the Hermeticism (and other mystic traditions) That works out okay for the feel of that game, but you might want to tone it down or skew it a little more towards something a little more Rosicrucian to get a more Order of Hermes feel. Or even subtract it almost entirely, except maybe for some Ex Misc folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T14:24:41-07:00","id":544288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/526192-have-you-run-owod-setting-with-nwod-2e-rules-tell-us-about-it-here#post526192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I even created a list of nWoD 2E-compatible Archid traits for the Mokol\u00e9.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems... daunting. It's possible to become around 800 meters tall in Archid, given eight purchases of Tall. It's not really too compatible with the focus that nWoD tends to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T19:53:53-07:00","id":544659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/526192-have-you-run-owod-setting-with-nwod-2e-rules-tell-us-about-it-here?p=538292#post538292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by awakening practices?</div> </div> </div> </div>By Awakening Practices, I mean that the dots in Awakening Arcana do different things at different levels than Ascension Spheres do. Furthermore, Awakening assumes that magic specifically works in a single unified way that Ascension eschews. Rotes are not nearly as important ( though fairly important) and magic generally requires specific spheres to be used in conjunction for specific effects. Foci are also given much more importance in Ascension than Awakening and Paradox works differently in terms of narrative effect. Look at the translation guide for more details.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T09:26:49-07:00","id":545396,"title":"","content":"I use Awakening magic system in my Omage, I love the setting but I never understood what the Spheres did. (Entropy is a special mess of its own)<br /> <br /> I will also use Beasts as Fomorian or Thallains if I do Ochangeling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}